<title>USA: Snyder expands securities repurchase.</title>
<headline>Snyder expands securities repurchase.</headline>
<dateline>FORT WORTH, Texas 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Snyder Oil Corp said Thursday its board had approved a $10 million expansion of its securities repurchase program, to a cumulative limit of $30 million.</p>
<p>Since the program began in May 1996, Snyder has repurchased over one million common shares and $4.1 million of subordinated notes, at a total cost of about $16 million, the company said.</p>
<p>Snyder said its share price does not fully reflect the values of its international assets, including a stake in Cairn Energy Plc.</p>
</text>
